WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:02.410
Your agent works for a week.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.330
Then it falls apart.

3
00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.810
The wrong account.

4
00:00:06.060 --> 00:00:07.630
It forgets what it learned.

5
00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:10.190
And nobody can say what it changed.

6
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.720
PassionCode.ai is the agent-agnostic

7
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.570
operating system for AI-native teams:

8
00:00:16.860 --> 00:00:20.610
a workplace where agents do the work,
and you see all of it.

9
00:00:20.940 --> 00:00:23.740
It runs on your machines, as open source,

10
00:00:23.780 --> 00:00:26.650
with the agents and
subscriptions you already have.

11
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:29.370
Their work leaves a record you can open.

12
00:00:29.820 --> 00:00:34.710
For you, one command sets up Fabric,
the tools around it and the skills,

13
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:37.090
and your coding agent can run it for you.

14
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.770
Fabric, in preview, is the home
for your projects and their agents.

15
00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:45.530
Your coding agent shows its
plan before it changes anything.

16
00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.870
Each tool works with Fabric, and on its own.

17
00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:53.690
Switchboard: each agent on the
account it should, limits in view.

18
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.370
Dashboards: state,
spend and control, in one window.

19
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.950
Observatory: what changed, with the evidence.

20
00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:04.050
Inbox, in preview:

21
00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:07.390
mail your agents answer
only within your rules.

22
00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.170
Agents connected to Fabric
share one project’s board,

23
00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:12.730
memory and hand-offs,

24
00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.070
so one picks up where another stopped.

25
00:01:15.480 --> 00:01:19.830
For an organization, we bring agents
onto your machines, connect them,

26
00:01:19.880 --> 00:01:22.670
and show what each one
cost and what it delivered.

27
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:25.830
Agents are easy to start and hard to keep.

28
00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:28.250
We are building what holds them together.
